@startuml
/' English-edition adaptation: Copyright 2026 kingle.zhuang. See NOTICE for upstream attribution. '/
' Regression from an actual course robustness diagram: Register Author in an
' online bookstore. Its authentic modeling defects are intentionally retained.
' Expected findings: entity-to-actor shortcut (database treated as actor),
' a god control absorbing behavior, directed arrows, and uncolored alternatives.
left to right direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Administrator" as ACT_Admin
actor "Database System" as ACT_BD

boundary "Main Menu" as B_Menu
boundary "Author Registration Form" as B_Form
boundary "Confirmation Message" as B_Confirm
boundary "Error Message" as B_Error

control "AuthorRegistrationManager" as C_Gestor

entity "Author" as E_Author
entity "Audit" as E_Audit

ACT_Admin --> B_Menu : 1. select Register Author
B_Menu --> C_Gestor : request form
C_Gestor --> B_Form : 2. show form
ACT_Admin --> B_Form : 3. enter author data
B_Form --> C_Gestor : submit captured data
C_Gestor --> E_Author : 5. validate and store
E_Author --> ACT_BD : persist record
C_Gestor --> E_Audit : record audit
C_Gestor --> B_Confirm : 7. generate confirmation
C_Gestor --> B_Error : FA-01 blank fields detected
B_Error --> ACT_Admin : show validation errors
ACT_BD --> E_Author : FE-03 persistence error
@enduml
